<p>Oil and gasoline prices jumped over the past week after the war involving Iran, the U.S., and Israel disrupted a key artery for global energy shipments in the Persian Gulf. Several outlets said tankers carrying roughly 20 million barrels of oil per day are now stuck because ships can’t safely transit the Strait of Hormuz, a narrow chokepoint bordered by Iran. In the United States, drivers felt the impact fast. AAA said the national average price for regular gasoline rose from $2.98 a week earlier to $3.41 on Saturday, after climbing from $3.25 on Thursday to $3.32 on Friday. Crude oil pushed above $90 a barrel as traders weighed tighter supply and higher shipping risk. The shock is rippling beyond the West, too. CBS News underscored China’s exposure to Persian Gulf supply routes, noting the conflict has disrupted flows of Iranian oil that factor heavily into China’s supply picture.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/O0GxUrcHwB0kPz5kfFm0xBRV8qTKT64pEKaG19xub8zmPFl6Y6rtOjDjRpDevjm7sbjohP35SkOWMNlj3YTdheHoiJUYE6GOvkijaWBIBs7tEV8uHpE5RI-Fhc5zrpy93gyES418xK8fWIqmHswANtaOKgmFZUQGwAimSOliOEnc98yjWiaBsriZioPya6hEVNyTm9pjqCeUKn23f7GM9u_Pv1g' alt='Energy-related scene amid the Iran crisis and market disruptions.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Europe gas spike: Natural gas prices in Europe rose even more sharply than U.S. gasoline prices as the conflict tightened supply expectations, according to Time’s roundup of market moves.</li><li>Price comparison: AAA said the last similar week-over-week jump in the national U.S. gas average came in March 2022, at the start of the Russia-Ukraine war.</li><li>Where it hits: Reports described missile or drone damage across much of the Middle East, helping explain why insurers and shippers are treating the route as unusually risky right now.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>AAA (U.S. motor club): AAA said the national average rose about 14% in a week and warned that when crude has traded around these levels in the past, the U.S. average pump price has been closer to about $3.80 a gallon—suggesting prices could keep climbing. (<a href='https://time.com/7383060/gas-prices-iran-war-oil/'>Time</a>)</li><li>Iran’s Revolutionary Guard: A spokesman said Iran did not close Hormuz and would keep it open to all traffic except U.S. and Israeli ships, which it would target if they transit the strait. (<a href='https://time.com/7383060/gas-prices-iran-war-oil/'>Time</a>)</li><li>CBS News (China focus): CBS cast the disruption as a stress test for China’s energy security, since Chinese buyers depend heavily on Persian Gulf routes and Iranian crude flows, both of which have been hit by the conflict. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/video/war-iran-exposes-chinas-reliance-oil-persian-gulf/'>CBS News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-07-0800/energy-oil-and-gas-prices-rapidly-rise-iran-war-shows-no-signs-letting'>Oil and gas prices rapidly rise as Iran war shows no signs of letting up</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/video/war-iran-exposes-chinas-reliance-oil-persian-gulf/'>War in Iran exposes China&#x27;s reliance on oil from Persian Gulf</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/oil-and-gas-prices-rise-rapidly-as-iran-war-escalates'>Oil and gas prices rise rapidly as Iran war escalates</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://time.com/7383060/gas-prices-iran-war-oil/'>Gas Prices Surge in U.S. as Iran War Chokes Global Oil Supply. What You Need To Know</a> - time.com</li></ul>